{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The artifacts that carry the distance question all describe one and the same trip: trip_id TRP-02817 appears on the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown alike; the trace's first fix (2026-08-10T07:28:09+08:00) is the recorded trip_started timestamp, and the fare was charged at 07:47:14, after the recorded trip end at 07:46:49. The rider's identification limb under POL-RD-08 is satisfied on the platform's own telemetry.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02817", "EV-GPS-02817", "EV-FARE-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider pleaded the governing field, and the governing field confirms the detour: POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the measure, the trace runs 14.39 km against the 12.0 km optimal stored on the trip record, and the excess is 2.39 km. The trip record's 14.4 km is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and under POL-RD-01 may not be cited for the threshold test; the rider has not cited it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02817", "EV-TRIP-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The establishment test is not met on the field as published, and the rider does not pretend otherwise: the trace excess of 2.39 km clears the absolute limb (well above 0.8 km) but is 19.92% of the 12.0 km optimal, some 10 metres short of the 20% limb, so POL-RD-01's percentage test fails and no deviation is established. The rider does not ask the tribunal to read 19.92% as 'greater than 20%', and does not press a distance refund as of right.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02817", "EV-TRIP-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only explanation — \"Minor detour because of a road works sign\" — cannot be weighed, and I disclose the impairment on its face: no traffic advisory covers this trip, EV-ADVIS-02817-01 being MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run, no closure-adjusted optimal can be produced, and under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 an uncited traffic assertion neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended route; the driver names no artifact and no clause at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02817-01", "EV-GPS-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-02"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this record excludes any part of the measured excess. The chat log holds 0 messages, so there is no rider instruction capable of engaging POL-RD-04; neither pickup_amended_at nor dropoff_amended_at is set and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 does not re-apply the threshold against amended endpoints; and vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply and 12.0 km remains the only optimal on the record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02817", "EV-TRIP-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the tribunal finds the establishment test satisfied, the refund is arithmetic and is 2.56 before rounding: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 12.0 + 0.28 x 16.0) x 1.0 — the surge multiplier read from the fare breakdown, which is where POL-RD-02 says it must be read — plus 0.80 platform fee, nil ERP, nil fixed surcharge, nil waiting fee, less nil promo, giving 18.08; refund = 20.64 - 18.08 = 2.56, payable rounded up to SGD 2.60.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02817", "EV-TRIP-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "That refund is neither de minimis nor full: 2.56 is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so this is not a NO_ACTION case on quantum, and it is 12.4% of the 20.64 charged, below the 90% share that would make it a FULL_REFUND; it is also far below the SGD 150 figure that forces escalation under POL-RD-10. On that arithmetic the rider's ask is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 2.60 out of the SGD 3.00 contested.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund_share_of_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No corroboration burden beyond the trace attaches to the rider's claim under POL-RD-08: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the four-or-more claims / one-or-fewer substantiated combination that would require independent corroboration for a sub-30% excess is simply not present here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the tribunal cannot reach confidence of 0.70 or better on a NO_ACTION ruling, POL-RD-10(1) requires ESCALATE, and on an escalation under POL-GEN-03 the disputed SGD 3.00 is held rather than collected — a materially better position for the rider than a ruling that leaves the whole 20.64 charged. The margin is exactly the size that makes that confidence arguable: the gate turns on a 10-metre shortfall measured over 113 fixes sampled every 10 seconds with no gaps, and the platform's own two published figures for the same distance (14.39 km and 14.4 km) differ by 0.01 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02817", "EV-TRIP-02817", "EV-FARE-02817"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the disputed trip (TRP-02817) ran 14.39 km on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02817) against a booked optimal of 12.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02817), a measured excess of 2.39 km. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern and requires BOTH limbs of the establishment test to pass: the excess must be greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km. The absolute limb passes (2.39 km), but the percentage limb does not: 2.39 km is 19.92% of 12.0 km, below the 20% gate. The trip record's rounded 14.4 km would give exactly 20.0% — still not 'greater than 20%', and in any event not the governing field. No route deviation is therefore ESTABLISHED, and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The 2.39 km excess is exactly the kind of minor detour the POL-RD-01 gate excludes from being refundable. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 113 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s — so none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is met, no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The only surviving route to money on a failed establishment test is a billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4), and there is nothing to correct: the fare ledger (EV-FARE-02817) carries no ERP gantry lines, no tolls and no airport surcharge, and every charge line reconciles to the trip record. The driver's note of a 'minor detour because of a road works sign' is not weighed: no traffic advisory covers this window (EV-ADVIS-02817-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and, under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08, an uncited traffic assertion neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended optimal; it equally does not create a deviation the numeric gate does not find. The rider's quantified alternative — a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 2.60 computed under POL-RD-02 (recomputed_fare 18.08 against charged_total 20.64) — never runs, because POL-RD-02 applies only where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01. The rider's request to escalate on confidence grounds does not fire: the deciding facts (the trace distance and the booked optimal) are carried by the unimpaired GPS trace and trip record, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and the ruling is well above the 0.70 floor; POL-RD-10(5) and (7) are also not engaged, as the driver cited no advisory identifier and the rider's own figures concede the gate fails. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION leaves the state exactly as it is: fare_breakdown.payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 stand, and the disputed SGD 3.00 is not refunded. The monetary effect is zero, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so no amount is held for reviewer release."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties agree on the decisive arithmetic, and so do I. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess distance is BOTH greater than 20% of the optimal route AND greater than 0.8 km. The governing measurement is gps_trace.trace_distance_km on EV-GPS-02817: 14.39 km against the 12.0 km optimal on EV-TRIP-02817. That is an excess of 2.39 km — it clears the absolute limb (2.39 > 0.8 km), but it is 19.92% of optimal, which is not 'greater than 20%'. The percentage limb fails, and because POL-RD-01 requires both limbs, no deviation is established. Using the trip record's rounded 14.4 km would give exactly 20.0%, still not 'greater than 20%'; POL-RD-01 in any event forbids citing that rounded copy for the threshold test. The margin is small (about 10 m over a 14.39 km trace), but both of the platform's own distance figures fall on the same side of the gate, so the result is not genuinely in doubt. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 113 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) are not met, no independent corroboration is required, and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. No exculpatory clause changes the result and none is needed: the chat log EV-CHAT-02817 holds 0 messages (no POL-RD-04 rider instruction); neither pickup nor dropoff was amended and amended_optimal_distance_km is null (POL-RD-05 inapplicable); and vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12 inapplicable), so 12.0 km remains the only optimal on the record. The driver's counterparty note — 'Minor detour because of a road works sign' — is an uncited traffic-cause assertion. No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-02817-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and, under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13, the assertion neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended optimal. Because the driver names no evidence ID for any advisory, POL-RD-13(1) treats this as a gap in the bundle rather than the POL-RD-10(5) contradiction, so it does not escalate the case. No billing-integrity correction is available under POL-RD-09(4): the fare ledger EV-FARE-02817 shows no ERP gantry lines, no tolls and no airport surcharge, and every line is meter arithmetic on the driven distance and time (14.4 km at $0.75/km plus 18.7 min at $0.28/min plus the $0.80 platform fee, surge multiplier 1.0 read from the fare breakdown). I have considered the rider's escalation request under POL-RD-10(1). The deciding fact — the 14.39 km trace on EV-GPS-02817 against the 12.0 km optimal on EV-TRIP-02817 — is carried by two independent weight-1.0 artifacts, so my confidence is capped at 1.0 and I am well above the 0.70 floor; POL-RD-10(1) is therefore not engaged. No other limb of POL-RD-10 fires either: identifiers match across all three artifacts (TRP-02817), no timestamps conflict or run backwards, the refund caps are nowhere near, and there is no mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength — both sides read the same arithmetic to the same result. The rider's conditional refund computation (recomputed fare 18.08, refund 2.56, payable 2.60) is correct arithmetic but is never reached, because POL-RD-02 only runs once a deviation is established and it is not. Ruling: NO_ACTION. The rider's claim is not supported by the evidence and the present state stands — the charge on EV-FARE-02817 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is left exactly as it is. No amount is refunded, no driver compensation is payable, and no clause produces a referral (POL-RD-06(c) needs a MATERIAL deviation and a driver pattern, neither of which exists; POL-RD-09(4) finds no phantom line). The disputed SGD 3.00 remains charged; the monetary effect (zero) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold, and this ruling is provisional with the POL-GEN-04 appeal route available to either party."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
